WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.335
 John, Tommy, congratulations.

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.538
You fellas have made
it into the final round

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.073
of this competition.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.576
It's time to step up your
games and make something worthy

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.177
of a "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.212
Now it's time to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:16.349
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:23.356
That weapon is the M 1832
foot artillery sword.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.791
You'll have four
days at your home

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.325
forge in which to
complete this challenge.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.128
At the end of your
four days, you'll

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.296
return and present your weapons
to our panel of expert judges.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.465
And after they've tested
the hell out of them,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.600
you guys will graduate
from child's play

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.136
to full-fledged "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:39.572
who wins a check for $10,000.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.540
Good luck, blade smiths.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.508
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:48.548
 Back here in my shop, here
in Gainesville, Texas, and I'm

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.019
taking on the M 1832
foot artillery sword.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:57.390
Today I want to get
the basics forged out.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.059
I'm using a car leaf
spring because I

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.060
use the leaf spring a lot.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.261
It makes a really good blade.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.596
It hardens really well.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.265
And it tempers really well.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:12.572
My secret weapon for moving
this metal, 8-pound hammer.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.640
Why?

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.973
Everything's bigger in Texas.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.676
That's why.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.478
My cane's a little off
center, so I had to fix it.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.046
I'm going to throw it
in the hydraulic press

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:22.615
to get it centered out.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.288
A little lower.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.791
She's a little ugly,
but she moves metal.

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:34.493
That's all that matters.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.528
Oh, perfect!

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:37.330
Woo-hoo!

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.335 line:0%
 Today I'm going to get
working on the handle.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.570
I'm going to be putting a lot of
my own twist into this weapon.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:48.775
So I'm making a
cast bronze handle.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.042 line:0%
In order to cast
this out of bronze,

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:51.710 line:0%
I've got to make a
positive, regardless.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.813 line:7%
So I could use any type of wood.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.181 line:7%
I can use clay.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.617 line:0%
This is just a really easy
material to work with.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.420
So the idea is that the metal is
going to travel down this tube.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.289
It's going to fill
this handle up.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.824
It's going to come down
the bottom, fill these up.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:10.196
And those will come out in
the mold as cast bronze.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.932
So this is a razor
tip wood burner.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.335
I'm going to use this to put
the dragon scale texture.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.804
This handle's going to
take longer than the blade

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.205
when it's all said and done.

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:22.441
But I think it's going
to be well worth it.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.075
Love it.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:23.877
Looks great.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.448 line:0%
 Yesterday I put it in
the forge and quenched.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:34.554
So I'm going to start
forging the garden pommel.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.056
Get her done!

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:40.459
Using a piece of round
stock mod steel--

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.529
nothing special, but it works.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.400
Looks good.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:50.235
So grinding is what
I'm going to do next.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:51.503
I'm here in round three.

00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:53.940
So happy I'm in round
three to begin with.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.509
And build, so far,
is going really good.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.746
[bleep]

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.182 line:0%
My blade goes through, and
it catches on the belt.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.284
It has happened to me
in a similar situation,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.787
where it's catastrophic.

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:10.022
This stupid thing.

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:14.427
I have a curl in my actual edge.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:18.531
I have to match the rest of the
edge to that lower point now.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:22.267
If I don't, this could
potentially be a weak spot.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.436
Just going to grind it out.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.038
Nothing I can do
other than that.

00:03:26.104 --> 00:03:27.941
Just gotta roll with adversity.

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:33.979 line:0%
 Today I have to finish
getting the handle cast.

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:35.548
I've got the original build.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:39.085
Now I need to make
the mold for it.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:44.156
So this is casting the sand
that holds shape really well.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:45.658
So what I'm going to
do is us pack this down

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:50.262
into the bottom of my flask,
lay my positive in there,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.365
and then pack it
in nice and tight.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:59.939
That's awesome.

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:01.273
So I've got my two halves now.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.943
Now I'm ready to put
them back together

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.479
and get them out to the foundry.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:09.615
I've got some bronze that I'm
going to start melting down.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.784
Once those get into
a molten state,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.185
then we'll be ready to pour.

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.154
The first time you're
casting any design,

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:16.822
there's always a lot of
issues that can come out.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.692
You know, the metal could
cool down too much before it

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.726
gets down to the bottom.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.427
The mold could
collapse on itself.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.764
It could just wreck inside,
and I don't know it.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.934
All right, if this
doesn't work, I'm screwed.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.704
A bad pour is going to set
me back at least half a day.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.406
I really don't have
that time to spend.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.085
Whoa!

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:51.924
That was 3,000 degrees of
metal hitting 60-degree water.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:52.925
Here she is.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.527
Hoo!

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.930
The cool thing about bronze is
that there's no carbon in it.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.434
So you don't have to worry about
cracking or anything like that.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.070
I came here to prove that
I can deliver more than I

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:06.572
did in the first two rounds.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.741
And I'm really excited to show
the judges what I've done.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.444
A $10,000 sword, if
I've ever seen one.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.249
 To find out what
kind of deadly force

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.152
your artillery
swords can supply,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.053
I will take your weapon,
deliver killing slashes

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:22.988
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:23.856
John, you're up first.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:24.490
You ready for this?

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.124
 Ready.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:29.662
[impact sounds]

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.649
 I like the beauty of an
all-metal construction.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:52.185
And the Damascus pattern
you have here is gorgeous.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.719
The weight-- it's all
the way in the handle--

00:05:53.785 --> 00:05:58.090
allows for a good recovery and
forward delivery of strikes.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.992
Your edges are very sharp.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:03.496
Every cut cuts deep, cuts to
the bone and into the organs.

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:06.865
And most importantly,
sir, it'll kill.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:07.900
 Thank you.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:08.901
 All right, Tom, your turn.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:09.669
You ready?

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.303
 Get her done.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:15.908
[impact sounds]

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:33.325
 The weight of your
weapon is all forward,

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.327
that it actually
takes a lot to pull

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.162
it away for a second strike.

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:40.833
But the thing that your beast
does have is a very sharp edge.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.835
Every cut is very deep.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.504
But it takes a lot of work
to control this beast.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:50.075
More importantly, though,
sir, it will kill.

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:52.177
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:06:52.277 --> 00:06:54.347
Now, why bring swords
to a gun range?

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.782
Well, so you two can join
one of our two clubs,

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.884
the "oh, my god, they broke
my blade with a bullet"

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:02.320
club or the
bulletproof sword club.

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:03.522
So to test your
blades, we've got

00:07:03.588 --> 00:07:05.023
our firearm locked in a vise.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.992
We've got your blade locked
in another vise down range.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.061
We're gonna fire one
round at that thing.

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:12.130
It should split that bullet
clean or, worst of all,

00:07:12.197 --> 00:07:13.966
see that blade shatter.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.001
John, you're up first.

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:15.801
You ready for this?
- Yep.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:16.735
 OK.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:17.403
Fire.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.504
[gunshot]

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:21.807
 Four holes.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:22.775
[gunshot]

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:31.516
 You can actually see top
and bottom where that bullet

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:33.085
went across your blade.

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:34.686
And you can see there's four
holes in the thing over there.

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.321
That's the lead
core and the jacket

00:07:36.421 --> 00:07:38.090
going in different directions.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.592
So you split that bullet nicely.

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:41.994
I don't see any
damage to your blade.

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:42.895
Well done.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:43.729
Good job.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:44.763
 Thank you.

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:46.031
 All right, Tommy,
are you ready for this?

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.032
 Let's do it.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:47.834
 Fire.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:51.737
 There we go.

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:59.579
 All right, Tommy, well,
your blade took some damage

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:00.779
in that bullet test.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.281
There's a chip in one spot.

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:05.284
And the other spot you can
actually hear my fingernail

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.651
catching on that roll.

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:09.588
Having said that, it
doesn't feel bad in my hand.

00:08:09.654 --> 00:08:11.857
But it is very heavy
for this type of sword.

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:15.228
But as far as the strength test
goes, as you can clearly see,

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.528
it took some damage.

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:18.130
 All right, blade
smiths, now that we

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:19.765
know your blades
can take a bullet,

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:21.434
it's time to find
out if they can cut.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:25.571
This is the sharpness
test, the shot bag slice.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:26.472
John, you're up first.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:27.205
You ready for this?

00:08:27.272 --> 00:08:28.040
 Yep.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:32.912
[impact sounds]

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.287
 Good job, man.

00:08:42.387 --> 00:08:43.188
 [chuckling]

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:44.289
 It is fun to wield.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:45.992
It is fun to move around.

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.326
It cuts with every slice.

00:08:48.393 --> 00:08:49.795
It will cut.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:50.762
 Thank you.

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:52.164
 All right, Tom,
it's your turn, sir.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:52.932
You ready?

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:54.200
 Let's do it.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:58.137
[impact sounds]

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.747
 Awesome.

00:09:08.847 --> 00:09:10.482
 All right, Tommy, on
the stationary cuts,

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:11.483
it cuts cleanly.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.052
It's a sharp blade.

00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:15.621
Now, when I'm moving around
and changing my balance because

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:17.322
of the weight of
the blade, it does

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:18.824
affect the way I'm cutting.

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:21.093
So some of the cuts are not
clean all the way through.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.495
There are some strands.

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:25.230
More importantly, your
weapon here, though a beast,

00:09:25.297 --> 00:09:28.166
it will cut.

00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:31.437
 John, Tommy, the judges have
made their final decision.

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:35.374
Our new "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:38.844
John, congratulations, you are
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:42.348
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:43.114
Good job, brother.

00:09:43.181 --> 00:09:44.683
 Thank you.

00:09:44.783 --> 00:09:46.152
It feels great to be the next
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:47.453
 Good job, brother.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.887
 I'm super proud of all
the work that I've done.

00:09:48.987 --> 00:09:51.823
I've come here and
done tasks that I never

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.492
would have expected
from myself, put

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:56.495
myself into challenges that I
never would have tried before.

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:59.398
And I've succeeded,
so I feel awesome.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:02.602
[theme music playing]

